# samples/06-MultiTenancy – start it with: dotnet run --project samples/06-MultiTenancy
@baseUrl = http://localhost:5106

### acme's endpoint
GET {{baseUrl}}/welcome
X-Tenant: acme

### globex's endpoint on the same route
GET {{baseUrl}}/welcome?name=Ann
X-Tenant: globex

### 404 – no tenant
GET {{baseUrl}}/welcome

### 404 – an endpoint of acme only
GET {{baseUrl}}/promo
X-Tenant: globex

### Shared: everybody
GET {{baseUrl}}/status

### ef-crud with a tenant column: acme's rows
GET {{baseUrl}}/products?sort=-price
X-Tenant: acme

### …globex creates one – stamped globex, "tenantId" in the body is ignored
POST {{baseUrl}}/products
X-Tenant: globex
Content-Type: application/json

{ "sku": "UMB-3", "name": "Umbrella", "price": 12, "stock": 5, "tenantId": "acme" }

###
GET {{baseUrl}}/products
X-Tenant: globex

### 404 – a request without a tenant never sees all rows
GET {{baseUrl}}/products

### Shared reference data
GET {{baseUrl}}/countries
X-Tenant: globex

### sql-query on acme's connection
GET {{baseUrl}}/reports/stock
X-Tenant: acme

### The tenant admin API: acme's endpoints only
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/tenants/acme/endpoints

### Created through globex's admin API – belongs to globex
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/tenants/globex/endpoints
Content-Type: application/json

{ "method": "GET", "route": "/promo", "processor": "response", "processorConfig": { "body": { "code": "GLOBEX10" } } }

###
GET {{baseUrl}}/promo
X-Tenant: globex

### Rejected: acme may only use the acme-reports connection
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/tenants/acme/endpoints/validate
Content-Type: application/json

{ "method": "GET", "route": "/reports/everything", "processor": "sql-query", "processorConfig": { "query": "SELECT * FROM \"Products\"" } }

### Tenants that own endpoints
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/endpoints/tenants

### OpenAPI per tenant
GET {{baseUrl}}/openapi/acme/dynamic.json

###
GET {{baseUrl}}/openapi/globex/dynamic.json
